  "corrections": [
    "HTTP 401 clears the browser session and returns to login instead of retaining stale workspace/group controls.",
    "A 100-second per-request limit covers response headers and body; explicit cancellation remains immediate and recoverable.",
    "The image E2E proof waits for the exact current scan path and visible layout before measuring; Firefox CI exposed a sample taken during a detached-canvas transition."
  ],
  "comparisons": [
    "All 12 downloaded content files are byte-identical. Complete index text differs only in its captured download-date field, which is the sole normalization.",
    "All cells of native partial-error XLSX are reconstructed for explanation; the browser deliberately prevents publishing that partial result.",
    "All cells of three complete 5000-person/150000-response native workbook checkpoints are paired with browser conversion. ZIP metadata is not normalized into a byte-identity claim.",
    "Code-generator retry validates all 2800 codes, alphabets, uniqueness and normalized workbook cells.",
    "Exclusive output lock is also tested against the real browser local-file helper on Windows CI; non-Windows runs explicitly skip that OS-specific test."
  ],
  "qualifiedDifferences": [
    "Native groups HTTP 500/401 silently display an empty list. Browser reports the failure and rolls back a failed ordinary selection; an expired session requires new login.",
    "Native response HTTP 500/503 may finish with zero or partial rows. Browser errors publish no partial download.",
    "Native cancellation waits for the current response/content file and can retain read data in its process. Browser aborts immediately and restores its prior database state.",
    "Native small ZIP save has no separately observable GUI cancellation checkpoint. Cell-conversion cancellation and an actual write-time exclusive lock/retry are directly observed; arbitrary interruption inside filesystem/ZIP writes is not claimed."
  ],
  "excludedPreparations": [
    "Initial TE10 reused retained state after cancellation; final TE10F is the isolated partial-failure run.",
    "First large CSV folder attempt preceded completed file transfer. The next generated input had a duplicate BOM. Both are excluded; final single-BOM input is byte-verified and recognized by the native GUI.",
    "The initial and repeated full large runs completed before a cancellation could be requested; they are completed baselines. The final cancel is captured while person rows are still being converted."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Synthetic data, no empirical study files.",
    "Finite fault cases and phase observations do not establish equality for arbitrary network failures, file sizes, operating systems or gesture histories."
  ]
}
